{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Migrate-vs-defer analysis (complements the migration inventory comment): reasons NOT to migrate immediately, all time-limited. (1) New required deps: mcp 2.0 hard-requires opentelemetry-api>=1.28 and an EXACT-pinned mcp-types (couples two dists in uv.lock), and replaces httpx with httpx2 — httpx/httpx-sse and pydantic-settings are no longer pulled in by mcp, so anything relying on them transitively must declare them. (2) sse-starlette floor jumps >=1.6 -> >=3.0 (two majors ride along). (3) Maturity: 2.0.0 shipped 2026-07-28 (days old); early-major regressions likelier than late 1.x, and the v1.x branch officially receives security fixes — our GHSA-9h52-p55h-vw2f DNS-rebinding protection is intact on 1.29. (4) Behavioral audits required beyond renames: lifespan becomes once-per-process (not per-session); sync def tools run on a worker thread; MCPError inside tools becomes a JSON-RPC error instead of isError=true; bare 'Host: localhost' (no port) now 421s under the auto-allowlist. (5) rebar-mcp is consumed externally — smoke-test protocol negotiation against real clients before flipping. RECOMMENDATION: stay on mcp>=1.28.1,<2 for now (already the landed state via ticket 1dfd change 1245); execute this ticket once mcp 2.0.x has a patch release or two rather than migrating on a .0. When executed, the port is mostly mechanical (FastMCP -> MCPServer at mcp.server.mcpserver, decorator API unchanged, auth/transport_security/mcp.types import paths unchanged) with four design-REVIEW points listed in the prior comment; no compat shim needed since we can drop <2 outright. OSS convergence: official-SDK MCPServer port is the standard path; PrefectHQ fastmcp is a separate ecosystem, not a migration target; compat shims (Kiln mcp_compat.py, mcp-hangar _sdk_compat.py) only matter for projects straddling both majors."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785725164779720001,"uuid":"4873c871-8bf5-4436-8ece-c4fe05592ae5"}